        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "A final observation before we end: your readers want you to write clearly, even simply—but not simplistically (see p. 16). Some argue that all sentences should be short, no more than fifteen words or so. But many mature ideas cannot be expressed so compactly. In Lessons 9 and 10 we look at ways to write longer sentences that communicate complex ideas but are still readable.",
